Why This Market Matters
Corn wet-milling is an integrated processing technology that separates corn into starch, gluten protein, fiber and oil fractions. Its importance extends across food manufacturing, biofuel production and specialty chemicals because processors can generate multiple commercial products from the same feedstock. Modernization, enzyme optimization, energy-efficiency initiatives and the development of higher-value protein and starch streams are increasingly influencing investment decisions.

